"Shows a small set of mutually exclusive shares as sectors of one complete whole.\n\nUse when: A single composition has only a few clearly different nonnegative parts. Readers mainly need a rough impression of each part’s share of the whole.\n\nAvoid when: Precise comparisons, many similar slices, or multiple compositions are required.\n\nVisual grammar: Sector angle and area encode component share of the total. Color and direct labels identify the parts.\n\nBuild: Calculate shares using a complete, explicit denominator. Order slices consistently and start from a simple reference angle. Draw a flat circle and place short part-and-percentage labels outside sectors with clear spacing.\n\nCheck: Check shares sum to 100% within rounding tolerance. Verify omitted categories are included in an explicit remainder. Confirm sector angles correspond to the numeric proportions.\n\nPitfalls: Three-dimensional perspective and exploded sectors distort apparent area. Prefer a sorted bar chart when slice sizes are similar or labels need crossing leader lines.\n\nExample: Show synthetic membership shares for four plans, with direct percentage labels and a clearly stated total membership count.\n\nAlternatives: Waffle chart, 100% stacked bar chart, Treemap."
